# Staging build config for the SPA — committed ON PURPOSE, same reasoning as .env.production:
# Vite INLINES VITE_* at build time, and a Clerk publishable key is public by definition
# (`pk_test_` + base64 of the Frontend API host). NEVER put a secret here.
#
# Selected by `vite build --mode staging` (Dockerfile ARG VITE_MODE, set by the `frontend-staging`
# entry in .github/workflows/cd-pipeline.yml), which is why this file exists instead of reusing
# .env.production: the instance must match the staging backend's CLERK_DOMAIN / CLERK_JWKS_URL
# (PLAN §3b) — the Development instance, NOT clerk.seekeru.tech. The SPA authenticates against the
# instance whose JWKS the backend trusts; pointing a staging SPA at the prod instance (or vice
# versa) fails auth in a way that looks like a backend bug.
#
# The pk below is derived from the Frontend API host (`pk_test_` + base64("<host>$")) and was
# verified against that host's /v1/environment endpoint. The shipped image is tagged
# `staging-<sha>`, never `latest` (see CD): an unqualified pull must stay the prod SPA.
VITE_API_BASE=/api
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_a25vd24tcG9sZWNhdC0xNi5jbGVyay5hY2NvdW50cy5kZXYk
